# User-facing UI copy

Settings labels, subtitles, helper text, empty states, and dialogs are for
**end users**. Tell them what the control does in everyday language.

## Do

- Write short, plain copy that answers “what is this for?” / “how do I use it?”
- Prefer concrete product language: chat, bubble, message, background, highlight
- Keep descriptions one short sentence when possible
- Match the user’s locale tone (中文自然口语；English clear and simple)

## Don't

- Do not write like code comments or internal docs
- Do not expose implementation terms: scaffold, token, ARGB, lerp, ColorScheme,
  surfaceContainer, accent weight, “defaults to X”, “opaque fill”, “narration”
- Do not explain architecture, fallbacks, or how the theme engine derives values
- Do not stack multiple technical clauses with semicolons

## Examples

```text
❌ Solid fill behind the chat when no image background is set.
✅ The chat page background when you haven’t set a picture.

❌ Quoted speech color inside bubbles; defaults to a distinct accent and bold weight.
✅ Quoted speech in messages. Shown in this color and bold.

❌ 气泡内引号对白的颜色；默认使用区分色并加粗
✅ 引号里说的话会用这个颜色，并加粗显示。
```
